  </tr>
  <tr > 
    <td><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> <strong>Events/Queries/By Event</strong></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr > 
    <td>&nbsp;</td>
  </tr>
  <tr > 
    <td height="308"> <table width="90%" height="294" border="1" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#3B6692">
        <tr> 
          <td height="292"> <div align="justify"></div>
            <div align="justify"></div>
            <div align="justify"> 
              <table width="90%" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
                <tr> 
                  <td width="30%" height="246"><img src="/datacenter/util/imgs/mn_menu_5_en.jpg" width="153" height="246"></td>
                  <td width="3%"></td>
                  <td width="67%"><div align="justify"> 
                      <p><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">This 
                        element allows users to obtain a list all reported events 
                        for a specific period. Other criteria such as country, 
                        division, unit, etc. can also be selected. <br>
                        After performing the query a list containing date, name 
                        and surname, division, subdivision and unit, as well as 
                        general classification, description and recommendations 
                        for the event will be displayed.<br>
                        It is possible to query details of the report by clicking 
                        on the date of the event.</font></p>
                    </div></td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </div></td>
        </tr>
      </table></td>
  </tr>
  <tr > 
    <td><font face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><strong>Events/Queries/By Type</strong></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr > 
    <td>&nbsp;</td>
  </tr>
  <tr > 
    <td><div align="justify"> 
        <table width="90%" height="295" border="1" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#3B6692">
          <tr> 
            <td height="293"> <div align="justify"> 
                <table align="CENTER" width="90%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
                  <tr> 
                    <td width="26%" height="246"><img src="/datacenter/util/imgs/mn_menu_6_en.jpg" width="153" height="246"></td>
                    <td width="2%">&nbsp;</td>
                    <td width="72%"><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="2" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">This 
                        element enables users to search for events by organizational 
                        criteria, period and event classification. If events are 
                        reported individually (specifying participant/driver), 
                        users must click on the field &#8220;individual&#8221;. 
                        If events are reported collectively, click on the field 
                        &#8220;collective&#8221;. According to the selected criteria 
                        the query will display a table with the number of accidents, 
                        incidents and fines, as determined by company. The table 
                        will also show the main consequence of the accident. <br>
                        The lack of reports or failure in the reporting process 
                        can interfere with totals presented. </font><br>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div align="justify"></div></td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div></td>
  </tr>
